  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Prashant Gupta vs Food Safety And Standards Authority Of ... on 8 August, 2025 Author: Amit Sharma Bench: Amit Sharma $~107 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + W.P.(C) 10368/2025 Prashant Gupta Through: Mr Gu versus Food Safety And Standards Authority Of India & Ors. .....Respond Through: Mr. Rakesh Chaudhary, Advocate R-1/Fssai.",
    "facts": "The authenticity of the order can be re-verified from Delhi High Court Order Portal by scanning the QR code shown above. d) Direct the Respondent No. 5 to conduct an inquiry against Respondent No. 2 and Respondent No. 3 for putting the life and health of petitioner and his wife, staffs, children, doctors, attendants, visitors, pregnant women and other into endangering; e) Direct Respondent No. 6 to Suspend, downgrade, or revoke Jaipur Golden Hospital accreditation manage by Respondent No. 2 and Respondent No. 3 for breach of NABH standards to protect the Article 21 of the Petitioner guaranteed by the Constitution of India; f) Direct the Respondent No. 7 to cancel health trade license of Jaipur Golden Hospital manage by Respondent No. 2 and Respondent no. 3 through inspection of the said premises, to protect the life, health and g) Direct the Respondent No. 8 to Monitor and evaluate food safety dignity of the petitioner; implementation against the Jaipur Golden Hospital for the safety and health of patients, staff, doctors, pregnant women, visitors, attendants, children, etc. and take disciplinary action against Respondent No. 2 and Respondent No. 3; h) Pass a strict warning along with Impose a heavy Penalty upon Jaipur Golden Hospital for such negligence and putting the life and health of the petitioner, his wife and other persons endangering; i) Direct the Respondent No. 2 and Respondent No. 3 to pay adequate compensation for such injury along with legal fees for this present Writ to the Petitioner; j) Pass such other or further order(s), direction(s), or relief(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem just and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case and in the favour of the Petitioner and against the Respondents in the interest of justice.\" 3. Learned counsel for the petitioner pointed out that various representations to the concerned Authorities have been filed with respect to issues raised in the present petition, However, no action has been taken by the Learned counsel for respondent no.1/FSSAI submits that the jurisdiction with respect to the present hospital is with respondent no. 8/Delhi State Food Commission.",
